DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270209
SUMMARY:Easy run 5 km after the swim - third run of the week. Short and g
 enuinely easy. Run FREQUENCY is what protects against injury\; distance 
 is what causes it.
DESCRIPTION:Week 2 of 12 - Base\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk
  test.\nFirst brick. Start the run within 5 minutes of racking the bike 
 and expect the first 10 min to feel wrong - it normalises by km 3 regard
 less of fitness. Get a bike fit booked: saddle height and cleat alignmen
 t are named ITBS contributors and you are about to add 3 h/week of ridin
 g.\n75 days to IRONMAN 70.3 Venice-Jesolo.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ironman703venicejesolo-w3-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134502Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270215
SUMMARY:Long ride 70 km steady (170 min)
DESCRIPTION:Week 3 of 12 - Base\nBuy the wetsuit now. Buy for BUOYANCY no
 t speed - beginner suits run 5 mm through core/hips/legs\, which directl
 y fixes the sinking-legs problem. Wetsuits give the biggest gain to inef
 ficient low-buoyancy swimmers\, i.e. you: 5-11%\, roughly 2-4 min over 1
 .9 km. Also buy neoprene BOOTIES - legal below 18.3 C and the water will
  be 15-17 C.\n69 days to IRONMAN 70.3 Venice-Jesolo.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
